Fundamental Consumer Protection Law clauses affecting daily purchases, with genuine case references: I. Key Sections of the Consumer Rights Law of the People's Republic of China

Right to Safe Products: Under Article 19, sellers must ensure goods pose no harm; violations grant buyers claim rights for damages, underscoring consumer security.

Refund and Replacement Entitlements: Article 24 mandates full refunds or exchanges for defective items within seven days, covering costs like shipping and repairs to uphold fairness.

Complaint Filing Deadlines: Article 22 imposes a two-year window for lodging grievances, encouraging prompt action to avoid evidence decay and ensure justice.

